{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ifMq3Z5HUVJ7o6EYXciPq","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule LiveVite.Components do\n     2→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     3→  Macros to generate component helper functions for rendering framework components.\n     4→\n     5→  Discovers component files in the given root directories and generates a function for each\n     6→  component name. The framework is detected from the file extension:\n     7→\n     8→    * `.vue` files generate helpers that render via `LiveVite.vue/1`\n     9→    * `.tsx` and `.jsx` files generate helpers that render via `LiveVite.react/1`\n    10→\n    11→  ## Examples\n    12→\n    13→  ```elixir\n    14→  # Discovers .vue, .tsx, and .jsx files in the given directories\n    15→  use LiveVite.Components, component_root: [\"./assets/vue\", \"./lib/my_app_web\"]\n    16→\n    17→  # Legacy option (equivalent to component_root for Vue-only discovery)\n    18→  use LiveVite.Components, vue_root: [\"./assets/vue\"]\n    19→  ```\n    20→\n    21→  ## Framework Configuration\n    22→\n    23→  By default, all frameworks are enabled. Use the `:frameworks` application config\n    24→  to control which frameworks are active:\n    25→\n    26→  ```elixir\n    27→  # config/config.exs\n    28→  config :live_vite, frameworks: [:vue, :react]\n    29→  ```\n    30→  \"\"\"\n    31→\n    32→  # Maps file extensions to their framework identifiers and the render function to call.\n    33→  @extension_framework %{\n    34→    \".vue\" => :vue,\n    35→    \".tsx\" => :react,\n    36→    \".jsx\" => :react\n    37→  }\n    38→\n    39→  @framework_extensions %{\n    40→    vue: [\".vue\"],\n    41→    react: [\".tsx\", \".jsx\"]\n    42→  }\n    43→\n    44→  @framework_render_fn %{\n    45→    vue: :vue,\n    46→    react: :react\n    47→  }\n    48→\n    49→  @active_frameworks Application.compile_env(:live_vite, :frameworks, [:vue, :react])\n    50→\n    51→  @doc \"\"\"\n    52→  Generates functions local to your current module that can be used to render framework components.\n    53→\n    54→  ## Options\n    55→\n    56→    * `:component_root` - List of directories to search for components (default: `[\"./assets/vue\"]`)\n    57→    * `:vue_root` - Legacy alias for `:component_root` (deprecated, prefer `:component_root`)\n    58→\n    59→  ## Examples\n    60→\n    61→  ```elixir\n    62→  use LiveVite.Components, component_root: [\"./assets/vue\", \"./lib/my_app_web\"]\n    63→  ```\n    64→  \"\"\"\n    65→  defmacro __using__(opts) do\n    66→    roots =\n    67→      Keyword.get(opts, :component_root) ||\n    68→        Keyword.get(opts, :vue_root, [\"./assets/vue\"])\n    69→\n    70→    roots = List.wrap(roots)\n    71→    active_frameworks = @active_frameworks\n    72→\n    73→    Enum.flat_map(roots, fn root ->\n    74→      if String.contains?(root, \"*\"),\n    75→        do:\n    76→          raise(\"\"\"\n    77→          Glob pattern is not supported in :component_root, please specify a list of directories.\n    78→\n    79→          Example:\n    80→\n    81→          use LiveVite.Components, component_root: [\"./assets/vue\", \"./lib/my_app_web\"]\n    82→          \"\"\")\n    83→\n    84→      discover_components(root, active_frameworks)\n    85→    end)\n    86→    |> Enum.uniq_by(fn {name, _framework} -> name end)\n    87→    |> Enum.map(fn {name, framework} -> name_to_function(name, framework) end)\n    88→  end\n    89→\n    90→  # Discovers component files in the given root directory for the active frameworks.\n    91→  # Returns a list of `{component_name, framework}` tuples.\n    92→  defp discover_components(root, active_frameworks) do\n    93→    extensions = extensions_for_frameworks(active_frameworks)\n    94→\n    95→    extensions\n    96→    |> Enum.flat_map(fn ext ->\n    97→      root\n    98→      |> Path.join(\"**/*#{ext}\")\n    99→      |> Path.wildcard()\n   100→      |> Enum.map(fn path ->\n   101→        name = Path.basename(path, ext)\n   102→        framework = Map.fetch!(@extension_framework, ext)\n   103→        {name, framework}\n   104→      end)\n   105→    end)\n   106→  end\n   107→\n   108→  defp extensions_for_frameworks(frameworks) do\n   109→    Enum.flat_map(frameworks, fn fw -> Map.get(@framework_extensions, fw, []) end)\n   110→  end\n   111→\n   112→  defp name_to_function(name, framework) do\n   113→    render_fn = Map.fetch!(@framework_render_fn, framework)\n   114→\n   115→    quote do\n   116→      def unquote(:\"#{name}\")(assigns) do\n   117→        assigns\n   118→        |> Map.put(:\"v-component\", unquote(name))\n   119→        |> LiveVite.unquote(render_fn)()\n   120→      end\n   121→    end\n   122→  end\n   123→end\n   124→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01K7pD6mdCqvMNeJej7ndSWB","session_id":"5ac10091-ab71-4c98-8d1a-2ddf315e307c","uuid":"61bf5733-67de-4544-9380-40253359997d"}
