{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014iRuNJBJYWEU3dKz6hNG3X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XUkMDciXzzG9K9KhARkMBp","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/ssr.ex"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":203,"cache_read_input_tokens":24482,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":203},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WC4gkhhqVGz7j5aErTxYzr","session_id":"5ac10091-ab71-4c98-8d1a-2ddf315e307c","uuid":"155b79b1-04a4-4104-8bab-8378d7ce8fec"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XUkMDciXzzG9K9KhARkMBp","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→defmodule LiveVite.SSR.NotConfigured do\n     2→  @moduledoc false\n     3→\n     4→  defexception [:message]\n     5→end\n     6→\n     7→defmodule LiveVite.SSR do\n     8→  @moduledoc \"\"\"\n     9→  A behaviour for rendering Vue components server-side.\n    10→\n    11→  To define a custom renderer, change the application config in `config.exs`:\n    12→\n    13→      config :live_vite, ssr_module: MyCustomSSRModule\n    14→\n    15→  Exposes a telemetry span for each render under key `[:live_vite, :ssr]`\n    16→  \"\"\"\n    17→\n    18→  require Logger\n    19→\n    20→  @type component_name :: String.t()\n    21→  @type props :: %{optional(String.t() | atom) => any}\n    22→  @type slots :: %{optional(String.t() | atom) => any}\n    23→  @type framework :: String.t()\n    24→\n    25→  @typedoc \"\"\"\n    26→  A render response which should have shape\n    27→\n    28→  %{\n    29→    html: string,\n    30→    preloadLinks: string\n    31→  }\n    32→  \"\"\"\n    33→  @type render_response :: %{optional(String.t() | atom) => any}\n    34→\n    35→  @callback render(component_name, props, slots, framework) :: render_response | no_return\n    36→\n    37→  @spec render(component_name, props, slots, framework) :: render_response | no_return\n    38→  def render(name, props, slots, framework \\\\ \"vue\") do\n    39→    case Application.get_env(:live_vite, :ssr_module, nil) do\n    40→      nil ->\n    41→        %{preloadLinks: \"\", html: \"\"}\n    42→\n    43→      mod ->\n    44→        meta = %{component: name, props: props, slots: slots, framework: framework}\n    45→\n    46→        body =\n    47→          :telemetry.span([:live_vite, :ssr], meta, fn ->\n    48→            {mod.render(name, props, slots, framework), meta}\n    49→          end)\n    50→\n    51→        with body when is_binary(body) <- body do\n    52→          case String.split(body, \"<!-- preload -->\", parts: 2) do\n    53→            [links, html] -> %{preloadLinks: links, html: html}\n    54→            [body] -> %{preloadLinks: \"\", html: body}\n    55→          end\n    56→        end\n    57→    end\n    58→  end\n    59→end\n    60→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WC4gkhhqVGz7j5aErTxYzr","session_id":"5ac10091-ab71-4c98-8d1a-2ddf315e307c","uuid":"ab248cbd-0a9d-477c-9441-8ec791fa3499"}
