{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TzUn2dtDuBmVdF3pk14pHT","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import type { Operation } from \"./jsonPatch.js\"\n     2→\n     3→/**\n     4→ * The state stored on the LiveView hook for a mounted framework component.\n     5→ * Each renderer manages its own `app` representation.\n     6→ */\n     7→export interface RendererState<TApp = unknown> {\n     8→  /** The reactive props object managed by the renderer */\n     9→  props: Record<string, any>\n    10→  /** The reactive slots object managed by the renderer */\n    11→  slots: Record<string, (...args: any[]) => any>\n    12→  /** The mounted framework application instance (opaque to the hook) */\n    13→  app: TApp | null\n    14→}\n    15→\n    16→/**\n    17→ * Context passed to the renderer when mounting a component on the client.\n    18→ */\n    19→export interface MountContext {\n    20→  /** The resolved framework component */\n    21→  component: unknown\n    22→  /** Initial props parsed from the DOM */\n    23→  props: Record<string, any>\n    24→  /** Initial slots parsed from the DOM */\n    25→  slots: Record<string, string>\n    26→  /** The DOM element to mount into */\n    27→  el: Element\n    28→  /** Whether this element was server-side rendered */\n    29→  ssr: boolean\n    30→  /** The LiveView hook instance, for composables/hooks to access */\n    31→  hook: any\n    32→}\n    33→\n    34→/**\n    35→ * Context passed to the renderer for server-side rendering.\n    36→ */\n    37→export interface SSRContext {\n    38→  /** The resolved framework component */\n    39→  component: unknown\n    40→  /** Props to render with */\n    41→  props: Record<string, any>\n    42→  /** Slot name -> HTML string mapping */\n    43→  slots: Record<string, string>\n    44→}\n    45→\n    46→/**\n    47→ * The framework renderer interface contract.\n    48→ *\n    49→ * Implement this interface to add support for a new frontend framework.\n    50→ * The renderer is responsible for:\n    51→ * - Converting raw props/slots into a reactive system the framework understands\n    52→ * - Mounting and unmounting component instances\n    53→ * - Applying incremental updates (props, slots, JSON patches) to mounted components\n    54→ * - Server-side rendering (optional)\n    55→ *\n    56→ * ## Lifecycle\n    57→ *\n    58→ * 1. `mount()` is called when the LiveView hook mounts. The renderer should:\n    59→ *    - Create reactive wrappers around props\n    60→ *    - Create slot render functions from HTML strings\n    61→ *    - Mount the framework component into the DOM element\n    62→ *    - Return a `RendererState` that the hook will store\n    63→ *\n    64→ * 2. `updateProps()` / `patchProps()` are called when the LiveView sends updates.\n    65→ *    The renderer must update the reactive props in-place to trigger re-renders.\n    66→ *\n    67→ * 3. `updateSlots()` is called when slot content changes.\n    68→ *\n    69→ * 4. `unmount()` is called when the LiveView hook is destroyed.\n    70→ *\n    71→ * ## Adding a New Framework\n    72→ *\n    73→ * ```ts\n    74→ * import type { FrameworkRenderer } from \"live_vite/renderer\"\n    75→ *\n    76→ * const reactRenderer: FrameworkRenderer = {\n    77→ *   name: \"react\",\n    78→ *   mount(ctx) { ... },\n    79→ *   updateProps(state, newProps) { ... },\n    80→ *   patchProps(state, operations) { ... },\n    81→ *   updateSlots(state, newSlots) { ... },\n    82→ *   unmount(state) { ... },\n    83→ * }\n    84→ * ```\n    85→ */\n    86→export interface FrameworkRenderer<TApp = unknown> {\n    87→  /** Human-readable name for debugging (e.g. \"vue\", \"react\", \"svelte\") */\n    88→  readonly name: string\n    89→\n    90→  /**\n    91→   * Mount a component into the DOM.\n    92→   *\n    93→   * Called during the LiveView hook's `mounted` lifecycle.\n    94→   * The renderer should create a framework app instance, set up reactivity,\n    95→   * and mount the component into `ctx.el`.\n    96→   *\n    97→   * @returns The renderer state to be stored on the hook\n    98→   */\n    99→  mount(ctx: MountContext): Promise<RendererState<TApp>> | RendererState<TApp>\n   100→\n   101→  /**\n   102→   * Replace all props with new values.\n   103→   *\n   104→   * Called when diff mode is disabled. The renderer should update the reactive\n   105→   * props object in-place (e.g. `Object.assign`) to maintain framework reactivity.\n   106→   */\n   107→  updateProps(state: RendererState<TApp>, newProps: Record<string, any>): void\n   108→\n   109→  /**\n   110→   * Apply JSON Patch operations to props.\n   111→   *\n   112→   * Called when diff mode is enabled, or for stream updates.\n   113→   * The renderer should apply patches in-place on the reactive props object.\n   114→   */\n   115→  patchProps(state: RendererState<TApp>, operations: Operation[]): void\n   116→\n   117→  /**\n   118→   * Update slot content.\n   119→   *\n   120→   * Called when the server sends new slot HTML. The `newSlots` map contains\n   121→   * slot name -> raw HTML string pairs. The renderer should convert these to\n   122→   * the framework's slot representation and update the reactive slots object.\n   123→   */\n   124→  updateSlots(state: RendererState<TApp>, newSlots: Record<string, string>): void\n   125→\n   126→  /**\n   127→   * Unmount and clean up the component.\n   128→   *\n   129→   * Called during the LiveView hook's `destroyed` lifecycle.\n   130→   * The renderer should tear down the framework app and release resources.\n   131→   */\n   132→  unmount(state: RendererState<TApp>): void\n   133→\n   134→  /**\n   135→   * Server-side render a component to an HTML string.\n   136→   *\n   137→   * Optional. If not implemented, SSR will be unavailable for this renderer.\n   138→   *\n   139→   * @returns HTML string (may include preload links separated by `<!-- preload -->`)\n   140→   */\n   141→  renderToString?(ctx: SSRContext): Promise<string>\n   142→}\n   143→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WC4gkhhqVGz7j5aErTxYzr","session_id":"5ac10091-ab71-4c98-8d1a-2ddf315e307c","uuid":"8dd7eb8a-b274-470d-8d1f-0a911903ef43"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K7pD6mdCqvMNeJej7ndSWB","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create a detailed report:\n\n## ~VUE Sigil Implementation Report\n\nBased on my analysis of the LiveVite codebase, here's how the `~VUE` sigil works:\n\n### Location and Definition\n\nThe sigil is defined in `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite.ex` at lines 354-379:\n\n```elixir\n@doc \"\"\"\nInlines a Vue single-file component inside a LiveView. This is the new recommended way over the `~V` sigil.\n\"\"\"\ndefmacro sigil_VUE(term, modifiers) do\n  do_sigil(term, modifiers, __CALLER__)\nend\n\ndefp do_sigil({:<<>>, _meta, [string]}, [], caller) do\n  path = \"./assets/vue/_build/#{caller.module}.vue\"\n\n  with :ok <- File.mkdir_p(Path.dirname(path)) do\n    File.write!(path, string)\n  end\n\n  quote do\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <LiveVite.vue\n      class={get_in(assigns, [:vue_opts, :class])}\n      v-component={\"_build/#{__MODULE__}\"}\n      v-socket={get_socket(assigns)}\n      v-ssr={get_in(assigns, [:vue_opts, :ssr]) != false}\n      {Map.drop(assigns, [:vue_opts, :socket, :flash, :live_action])}\n    />\n    \"\"\"\n  end\nend\n```\n\n### How It Works\n\n1. **Macro Invocation**: When you write `~VUE\"\"\"...\"\"\"` in an Elixir/HEEX template, it calls `sigil_VUE/2`\n\n2. **File Generation**: The sigil writes the Vue component string to disk at:\n   ```\n   ./assets/vue/_build/#{MODULE_NAME}.vue\n   ```\n   This dynamically generates a `.vue` file in the `_build` directory with the module name as the filename.\n\n3. **Component Registration**: After writing the file, the sigil generates an inline HEEX template that:\n   - Calls the `vue/1` component function with specific attributes\n   - Sets `v-component` to `\"_build/#{__MODULE__}\"` so the component resolver can find the generated file\n   - Extracts socket and options from the assigns using helper functions\n\n4. **Helper Functions** (lines 341-346):\n   ```elixir\n   def get_socket(assigns) do\n     case get_in(assigns, [:vue_opts, :socket]) || assigns[:socket] do\n       %LiveView.Socket{} = socket -> socket\n       _ -> nil\n     end\n   end\n   ```\n   This retrieves the LiveView socket from either `assigns.vue_opts.socket` or `assigns.socket`.\n\n5. **Attribute Handling**: The sigil:\n   - Extracts `class` from `assigns.vue_opts.class`\n   - Extracts `ssr` setting from `assigns.vue_opts.ssr` (defaults to true)\n   - Passes all other assigns as props to the Vue component\n   - Filters out internal attributes: `vue_opts`, `socket`, `flash`, `live_action`\n\n### Deprecated ~V Sigil\n\nThere's also a deprecated `~V` sigil (lines 349-352) that works identically but is marked for removal:\n\n```elixir\n@doc false\n@deprecated \"~V sigil is deprecated, please use ~VUE instead.\"\ndefmacro sigil_V(term, modifiers) do\n  do_sigil(term, modifiers, __CALLER__)\nend\n```\n\n### Files and Directory Structure\n\n**Generated Files**:\n- Vue components written to: `/assets/vue/_build/{ModuleName}.vue`\n- Tracked in `.gitignore` via line 282 of the install task: `_build/`\n\n**Key Components Involved**:\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite.ex` - Sigil definitions\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/components.ex` - Component helper generation\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/encoder.ex` - Props encoding\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/slots.ex` - Slot handling\n\n### Usage Pattern\n\nIn a LiveView:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyLive do\n  use MyAppWeb, :live_view\n\n  def render(assigns) do\n    ~VUE\"\"\"\n    <template>\n      <div>Hello {{ name }}</div>\n    </template>\n    \n    <script setup>\n      defineProps({ name: String })\n    </script>\n    \"\"\"\n  end\nend\n```\n\nThis generates:\n1. `./assets/vue/_build/Elixir.MyLive.vue` file with the template\n2. An inline HEEX component that renders it with the proper LiveView integration\n\n### Configuration Options\n\nVia `assigns.vue_opts`:\n- `ssr` - Enable/disable server-side rendering (defaults to true)\n- `class` - CSS classes to apply to the wrapper\n- `socket` - LiveView socket (can also be passed as top-level `assigns.socket`)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: adbd72f (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 41331\ntool_uses: 13\nduration_ms: 27746</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ac10091-ab71-4c98-8d1a-2ddf315e307c","uuid":"e8775c37-0a64-4039-93f2-1063990202b4","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand the current ~VUE sigil implementation in this Elixir project. Please find and read:\n\n1. The main `live_vite.ex` file that defines the ~VUE sigil\n2. The `components.ex` file that renders the vue component\n3. Any test files related to the sigil\n4. Any references to \"sigil\" across the codebase\n\nReport back the full contents of relevant files and how the sigil currently works.","agentId":"adbd72f","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create a detailed report:\n\n## ~VUE Sigil Implementation Report\n\nBased on my analysis of the LiveVite codebase, here's how the `~VUE` sigil works:\n\n### Location and Definition\n\nThe sigil is defined in `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite.ex` at lines 354-379:\n\n```elixir\n@doc \"\"\"\nInlines a Vue single-file component inside a LiveView. This is the new recommended way over the `~V` sigil.\n\"\"\"\ndefmacro sigil_VUE(term, modifiers) do\n  do_sigil(term, modifiers, __CALLER__)\nend\n\ndefp do_sigil({:<<>>, _meta, [string]}, [], caller) do\n  path = \"./assets/vue/_build/#{caller.module}.vue\"\n\n  with :ok <- File.mkdir_p(Path.dirname(path)) do\n    File.write!(path, string)\n  end\n\n  quote do\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <LiveVite.vue\n      class={get_in(assigns, [:vue_opts,