irectory Structure\n\n**Generated Files**:\n- Vue components written to: `/assets/vue/_build/{ModuleName}.vue`\n- Tracked in `.gitignore` via line 282 of the install task: `_build/`\n\n**Key Components Involved**:\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite.ex` - Sigil definitions\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/components.ex` - Component helper generation\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/encoder.ex` - Props encoding\n- `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/slots.ex` - Slot handling\n\n### Usage Pattern\n\nIn a LiveView:\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyLive do\n  use MyAppWeb, :live_view\n\n  def render(assigns) do\n    ~VUE\"\"\"\n    <template>\n      <div>Hello {{ name }}</div>\n    </template>\n    \n    <script setup>\n      defineProps({ name: String })\n    </script>\n    \"\"\"\n  end\nend\n```\n\nThis generates:\n1. `./assets/vue/_build/Elixir.MyLive.vue` file with the template\n2. An inline HEEX component that renders it with the proper LiveView integration\n\n### Configuration Options\n\nVia `assigns.vue_opts`:\n- `ssr` - Enable/disable server-side rendering (defaults to true)\n- `class` - CSS classes to apply to the wrapper\n- `socket` - LiveView socket (can also be passed as top-level `assigns.socket`)"}],"totalDurationMs":27746,"totalTokens":41331,"totalToolUseCount":13,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3092,"cache_read_input_tokens":36946,"output_tokens":1287,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3092,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0}}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WC4gkhhqVGz7j5aErTxYzr","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now let me create a comprehensive summary document based on my findings. Let me compile all the key information:\n\n## Summary: Framework Dispatch Patterns in LiveVite\n\nI've thoroughly analyzed the LiveVite project and found comprehensive patterns for framework-specific rendering. Here's what I discovered:\n\n### 1. **Elixir-Side Framework Dispatch**\n\n**Main Module: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite.ex`**\n\nThe project has **already implemented React support** alongside Vue:\n\n```elixir\n@doc \"\"\"\nRenders a React component within Phoenix LiveView.\nSets `v-framework` to `\"react\"` and delegates to the shared rendering pipeline.\n\"\"\"\ndef react(assigns) do\n  assigns\n  |> Map.put(:\"v-framework\", \"react\")\n  |> vue()\nend\n\ndef vue(assigns) do\n  # Extracts framework: defaults to \"vue\"\n  framework = Map.get(assigns, :\"v-framework\", \"vue\")\n  \n  # ... rendering logic ...\n  \n  ~H\"\"\"\n  <div\n    id={assigns[:id] || id(@__component_name)}\n    data-name={@__component_name}\n    data-framework={@__framework}  # <-- Framework dispatch attribute\n    data-props={\"#{json(Encoder.encode(@props))}\"}\n    ...\n  >\n  \"\"\"\nend\n```\n\n**Key Pattern:**\n- The `react/1` function simply sets `v-framework=\"react\"` and delegates to `vue/1`\n- The shared `vue/1` function renders a div with `data-framework` attribute\n- The attribute value is passed to the template as `data-framework={@__framework}`\n\n### 2. **Component Discovery & Framework-Specific Helpers**\n\n**File: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/components.ex`**\n\nThe project auto-discovers components and generates framework-specific helper functions:\n\n```elixir\n@extension_framework %{\n  \".vue\" => :vue,\n  \".tsx\" => :react,\n  \".jsx\" => :react\n}\n\ndefmacro __using__(opts) do\n  # Discovers .vue, .tsx, .jsx files\n  discover_components(root, active_frameworks)\n  # Generates a function for each component\n  |> Enum.map(fn {name, framework} -> name_to_function(name, framework) end)\nend\n\ndefp name_to_function(name, framework) do\n  quote do\n    def unquote(:\"#{name}\")(assigns) do\n      assigns\n      |> Map.put(:\"v-component\", unquote(name))\n      |> LiveVite.unquote(render_fn)()  # Calls LiveVite.vue() or LiveVite.react()\n    end\n  end\nend\n```\n\n**Usage Pattern:**\n```elixir\nuse LiveVite.Components, component_root: [\"./assets/vue\", \"./lib/my_app_web\"]\n# Generates: Counter(), NestedComponent(), etc. that auto-dispatch to correct renderer\n```\n\n### 3. **Sigil Pattern**\n\n**File: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite.ex` (lines 354-379)**\n\nThere is **no `~REACT` sigil** currently defined. Only `~VUE` (and deprecated `~V`):\n\n```elixir\n@doc \"\"\"\nInlines a Vue single-file component inside a LiveView.\n\"\"\"\ndefmacro sigil_VUE(term, modifiers) do\n  do_sigil(term, modifiers, __CALLER__)\nend\n\ndefp do_sigil({:<<>>, _meta, [string]}, [], caller) do\n  path = \"./assets/vue/_build/#{caller.module}.vue\"\n  \n  with :ok <- File.mkdir_p(Path.dirname(path)) do\n    File.write!(path, string)\n  end\n  \n  quote do\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <LiveVite.vue\n      class={get_in(assigns, [:vue_opts, :class])}\n      v-component={\"_build/#{__MODULE__}\"}\n      v-socket={get_socket(assigns)}\n      ...\n    />\n    \"\"\"\n  end\nend\n```\n\n**Note:** The sigil currently only supports Vue. A `~REACT` sigil would need to be added to support inline React components.\n\n### 4. **Server-Side Rendering (SSR) - Framework Agnostic**\n\n**File: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/ssr.ex`**\n\nThe SSR layer is already framework-agnostic:\n\n```elixir\n@type framework :: String.t()\n\n@callback render(component_name, props, slots, framework) :: render_response | no_return\n\ndef render(name, props, slots, framework \\\\ \"vue\") do\n  case Application.get_env(:live_vite, :ssr_module, nil) do\n    nil -> %{preloadLinks: \"\", html: \"\"}\n    \n    mod ->\n      meta = %{component: name, props: props, slots: slots, framework: framework}\n      :telemetry.span([:live_vite, :ssr], meta, fn ->\n        {mod.render(name, props, slots, framework), meta}\n      end)\n  end\nend\n```\n\nThe SSR module callback receives the `framework` parameter and can dispatch accordingly.\n\n### 5. **Client-Side Framework Dispatch**\n\n**File: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/assets/hooks.ts`**\n\nThe hooks layer uses the `data-framework` attribute for runtime dispatch:\n\n```typescript\nexport const getMultiRendererHook = (\n  renderers: Record<string, RendererEntry>,\n): Hook => {\n  const resolveRenderer = (el: HTMLElement): RendererEntry => {\n    const framework = el.getAttribute(\"data-framework\")\n    \n    if (framework && renderers[framework]) {\n      return renderers[framework]\n    }\n    \n    // Fallback: if only one renderer is registered, use it\n    if (!framework && rendererNames.length === 1) {\n      return renderers[rendererNames[0]]\n    }\n    \n    throw new Error(`Unknown framework \"${framework}\"...`)\n  }\n  \n  return {\n    async mounted() {\n      const { renderer, resolve } = resolveRenderer(this.el)\n      const componentName = this.el.getAttribute(\"data-name\")\n      const component = await resolve(componentName)\n      \n      const state = await renderer.mount({\n        component,\n        props: getProps(this.el, this.liveSocket),\n        slots: getRawSlots(this.el),\n        el: this.el,\n        ssr: this.el.getAttribute(\"data-ssr\") === \"true\",\n        hook: this,\n      })\n    },\n    ...\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 6. **Framework Renderer Interface**\n\n**File: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/assets/renderer.ts`**\n\nAll frameworks implement the same contract:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface FrameworkRenderer<TApp = unknown> {\n  readonly name: string\n  mount(ctx: MountContext): Promise<RendererState<TApp>>\n  updateProps(state: RendererState<TApp>, newProps: Record<string, any>): void\n  patchProps(state: RendererState<TApp>, operations: Operation[]): void\n  updateSlots(state: RendererState<TApp>, newSlots: Record<string, string>): void\n  unmount(state: RendererState<TApp>): void\n  renderToString?(ctx: SSRContext): Promise<string>\n}\n```\n\n### 7. **Framework Configuration**\n\n**File: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/components.ex` (line 49)**\n\nActive frameworks are configurable:\n\n```elixir\n@active_frameworks Application.compile_env(:live_vite, :frameworks, [:vue, :react])\n```\n\nCan be set in `config.exs`:\n```elixir\nconfig :live_vite, frameworks: [:vue, :react]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Findings\n\n1. **React support is already implemented** at the Elixir level via the `react/1` component function and auto-discovered `.tsx`/`.jsx` files\n2. **Framework dispatch flows through `data-framework` attribute** - set on the server in Elixir, read on the client in TypeScript\n3. **No `~REACT` sigil exists** - only `~VUE` is available for inline components\n4. **Client-side is fully multi-framework ready** - uses `getMultiRendererHook()` for dispatcher, `getRendererHook()` for single-renderer setups\n5. **SSR is framework-agnostic** - receives framework name and delegates to configured SSR module\n6. **Component discovery auto-routes** - `.vue` files call `vue()`, `.tsx`/`.jsx` files call `react()`\n\nThe architecture is clean and extensible - adding new frameworks would only require implementing the `FrameworkRenderer` interface on the client side."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: aec8182 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 33814\ntool_uses: 18\nduration_ms: 44247</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ac10091-ab71-4c98-8d1a-2ddf315e307c","uuid":"f58112f5-3195-44e5-af0f-0196a1e9f384","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Look at the Astro reference project at /home/andre/Documents/scratch/astro for any patterns related to framework-specific sigils, component rendering, or how React components are handled. Also check if there's any existing ~REACT sigil or framework dispatch pattern.\n\nSpecifically look for:\n1. Any Elixir files that handle React rendering\n2. Any sigil definitions\n3. How components are rendered with framework attributes\n\nReport back what you find.","agentId":"aec8182","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now let me create a comprehensive summary document based on my findings. Let me compile all the key information:\n\n## Summary: Framework Dispatch Patterns in LiveVite\n\nI've thoroughly analyzed the LiveVite project and found comprehensive patterns for framework-specific rendering. Here's what I discovered:\n\n### 1. **Elixir-Side Framework Dispatch**\n\n**Main Module: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite.ex`**\n\nThe project has **already implemented React support** alongside Vue:\n\n```elixir\n@doc \"\"\"\nRenders a React component within Phoenix LiveView.\nSets `v-framework` to `\"react\"` and delegates to the shared rendering pipeline.\n\"\"\"\ndef react(assigns) do\n  assigns\n  |> Map.put(:\"v-framework\", \"react\")\n  |> vue()\nend\n\ndef vue(assigns) do\n  # Extracts framework: defaults to \"vue\"\n  framework = Map.get(assigns, :\"v-framework\", \"vue\")\n  \n  # ... rendering logic ...\n  \n  ~H\"\"\"\n  <div\n    id={assigns[:id] || id(@__component_name)}\n    data-name={@__component_name}\n    data-framework={@__framework}  # <-- Framework dispatch attribute\n    data-props={\"#{json(Encoder.encode(@props))}\"}\n    ...\n  >\n  \"\"\"\nend\n```\n\n**Key Pattern:**\n- The `react/1` function simply sets `v-framework=\"react\"` and delegates to `vue/1`\n- The shared `vue/1` function renders a div with `data-framework` attribute\n- The attribute value is passed to the template as `data-framework={@__framework}`\n\n### 2. **Component Discovery & Framework-Specific Helpers**\n\n**File: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/components.ex`**\n\nThe project auto-discovers components and generates framework-specific helper functions:\n\n```elixir\n@extension_framework %{\n  \".vue\" => :vue,\n  \".tsx\" => :react,\n  \".jsx\" => :react\n}\n\ndefmacro __using__(opts) do\n  # Discovers .vue, .tsx, .jsx files\n  discover_components(root, active_frameworks)\n  # Generates a function for each component\n  |> Enum.map(fn {name, framework} -> name_to_function(name, framework) end)\nend\n\ndefp name_to_function(name, framework) do\n  quote do\n    def unquote(:\"#{name}\")(assigns) do\n      assigns\n      |> Map.put(:\"v-component\", unquote(name))\n      |> LiveVite.unquote(render_fn)()  # Calls LiveVite.vue() or LiveVite.react()\n    end\n  end\nend\n```\n\n**Usage Pattern:**\n```elixir\nuse LiveVite.Components, component_root: [\"./assets/vue\", \"./lib/my_app_web\"]\n# Generates: Counter(), NestedComponent(), etc. that auto-dispatch to correct renderer\n```\n\n### 3. **Sigil Pattern**\n\n**File: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite.ex` (lines 354-379)**\n\nThere is **no `~REACT` sigil** currently defined. Only `~VUE` (and deprecated `~V`):\n\n```elixir\n@doc \"\"\"\nInlines a Vue single-file component inside a LiveView.\n\"\"\"\ndefmacro sigil_VUE(term, modifiers) do\n  do_sigil(term, modifiers, __CALLER__)\nend\n\ndefp do_sigil({:<<>>, _meta, [string]}, [], caller) do\n  path = \"./assets/vue/_build/#{caller.module}.vue\"\n  \n  with :ok <- File.mkdir_p(Path.dirname(path)) do\n    File.write!(path, string)\n  end\n  \n  quote do\n    ~H\"\"\"\n    <LiveVite.vue\n      class={get_in(assigns, [:vue_opts, :class])}\n      v-component={\"_build/#{__MODULE__}\"}\n      v-socket={get_socket(assigns)}\n      ...\n    />\n    \"\"\"\n  end\nend\n```\n\n**Note:** The sigil currently only supports Vue. A `~REACT` sigil would need to be added to support inline React components.\n\n### 4. **Server-Side Rendering (SSR) - Framework Agnostic**\n\n**File: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/ssr.ex`**\n\nThe SSR layer is already framework-agnostic:\n\n```elixir\n@type framework :: String.t()\n\n@callback render(component_name, props, slots, framework) :: render_response | no_return\n\ndef render(name, props, slots, framework \\\\ \"vue\") do\n  case Application.get_env(:live_vite, :ssr_module, nil) do\n    nil -> %{preloadLinks: \"\", html: \"\"}\n    \n    mod ->\n      meta = %{component: name, props: props, slots: slots, framework: framework}\n      :telemetry.span([:live_vite, :ssr], meta, fn ->\n        {mod.render(name, props, slots, framework), meta}\n      end)\n  end\nend\n```\n\nThe SSR module callback receives the `framework` parameter and can dispatch accordingly.\n\n### 5. **Client-Side Framework Dispatch**\n\n**File: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/assets/hooks.ts`**\n\nThe hooks layer uses the `data-framework` attribute for runtime dispatch:\n\n```typescript\nexport const getMultiRendererHook = (\n  renderers: Record<string, RendererEntry>,\n): Hook => {\n  const resolveRenderer = (el: HTMLElement): RendererEntry => {\n    const framework = el.getAttribute(\"data-framework\")\n    \n    if (framework && renderers[framework]) {\n      return renderers[framework]\n    }\n    \n    // Fallback: if only one renderer is registered, use it\n    if (!framework && rendererNames.length === 1) {\n      return renderers[rendererNames[0]]\n    }\n    \n    throw new Error(`Unknown framework \"${framework}\"...`)\n  }\n  \n  return {\n    async mounted() {\n      const { renderer, resolve } = resolveRenderer(this.el)\n      const componentName = this.el.getAttribute(\"data-name\")\n      const component = await resolve(componentName)\n      \n      const state = await renderer.mount({\n        component,\n        props: getProps(this.el, this.liveSocket),\n        slots: getRawSlots(this.el),\n        el: this.el,\n        ssr: this.el.getAttribute(\"data-ssr\") === \"true\",\n        hook: this,\n      })\n    },\n    ...\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 6. **Framework Renderer Interface**\n\n**File: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/assets/renderer.ts`**\n\nAll frameworks implement the same contract:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface FrameworkRenderer<TApp = unknown> {\n  readonly name: string\n  mount(ctx: MountContext): Promise<RendererState<TApp>>\n  updateProps(state: RendererState<TApp>, newProps: Record<string, any>): void\n  patchProps(state: RendererState<TApp>, operations: Operation[]): void\n  updateSlots(state: RendererState<TApp>, newSlots: Record<string, string>): void\n  unmount(state: RendererState<TApp>): void\n  renderToString?(ctx: SSRContext): Promise<string>\n}\n```\n\n### 7. **Framework Configuration**\n\n**File: `/home/andre/Documents/scratch/live_vue/lib/live_vite/components.ex` (line 49)**\n\nActive frameworks are configurable:\n\n```elixir\n@active_frameworks Application.compile_env(:live_vite, :frameworks, [:vue, :react])\n```\n\nCan be set in `config.exs`:\n```elixir\nconfig :live_vite, frameworks: [:vue, :react]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Findings\n\n1. **React support is already implemented** at the Elixir level via the `react/1` component function and auto-discovered `.tsx`/`.jsx` files\n2. **Framework dispatch flows through `data-framework` attribute** - set on the server in Elixir, read on the client in TypeScript\n3. **No `~REACT` sigil exists** - only `~VUE` is available for inline components\n4. **Client-side is fully multi-framework ready** - uses `getMultiRendererHook()` for dispatcher, `getRendererHook()` for single-renderer setups\n5. **SSR is framework-agnostic** - receives framework name and delegates to configured SSR module\n6. **Component discovery auto-routes** - `.vue` files call `vue()`, `.tsx`/`.jsx` files call `react()`\n\nThe architecture is clean and extensible - adding new frameworks would only require implementing the `FrameworkRenderer` interface on the client side."}],"totalDurationMs":44247,"totalTokens":33814,"totalToolUseCount":18,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1997,"cache_read_input_tokens":29584,"output_tokens":2233,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1997,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0}}}}
