f v-component v-framework v-socket __changed__ __given__\"a,\n    do: :special\n\n  defp normalize_key(_key, [%{__slot__: _}]), do: :slots\n  defp normalize_key(key, val) when is_atom(key), do: key |> to_string() |> normalize_key(val)\n  defp normalize_key(\"v-on:\" <> key, _val), do: {:handlers, key}\n  defp normalize_key(_key, %LiveStream{}), do: :streams\n  defp normalize_key(_key, _val), do: :props\n\n  defp key_changed(%{__changed__: nil}, _key), do: true","numLines":20,"startLine":290,"totalLines":427}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01N71xFxAuSyxLqtprLbaChk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`v-framework` is in the special keys list on line 300, so it won't leak into props. The `Map.drop` in the sigil drops `vue_opts`, `socket`, `flash`, `live_action` — but `v-framework` will be passed both via the explicit attribute and through the `Map.drop(assigns, ...)` spread. However, since `v-framework` is set explicitly on the element, the explicit value will win (HEEx gives precedence to explicit attributes over spreads, or it might cause a compile error for duplicate attributes).\n\nWait, actually the sigil uses `{Map.drop(assigns, [:vue_opts, :socket, :flash, :live_action])}` which spreads *all remaining assigns* as attributes, including any user-provided `v-framework`. But the sigil also sets `v-framework` explicitly. This could cause a duplicate attribute issue.\n\nLooking at the original `~VUE` sigil, it didn't pass `v-framework` at all, and it relied on the default in `vue/1`. The `Map.drop` would not include `v-framework` in the spread since the user wouldn't set it when using the sigil.\n\nThe issue is: when the sigil generates the HEEx, the assigns come from the LiveView's assigns (like `@count`, `@name`, etc.) — they wouldn't normally have `v-framework` in them. So in practice, `v-framework` would only appear from the explicit attribute. This is safe.\n\nBut to be extra safe and consistent with the pattern, I should also drop `v-framework` from the spread, along with the other framework-internal keys. Actually, looking more carefully, the original `~VUE` sigil's `Map.drop` list was designed for the LiveView assigns (dropping `vue_opts`, `socket`, `flash`, `live_action`). The `v-framework` wouldn't be in those assigns. So this is fine as-is.\n\nNow let me also check if the `vue_opts` key should be renamed to something more generic for the `~REACT` case. Looking at the sigil, `vue_opts` is used for:\n- `assigns.vue_opts.class` → CSS class\n- `assigns.vue_opts.socket` → socket\n- `assigns.vue_opts.ssr` → SSR flag\n\nFor backward compatibility, keeping `vue_opts` for both sigils is fine — this is the established API. The name is a bit misleading for React but changing it would break existing users.\n\nLet me now update the `@moduledoc` to mention both sigils."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":36051,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":702},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ac10091-ab71-4c98-8d1a-2ddf315e307c","uuid":"f12bce18-5426-499e-bae8-05dd454dc96a"}
